# Markdown line length policy

When creating or editing Markdown, do not enforce fixed line-length limits (for example 80 characters).

## Required behavior

1. Prioritize readability and natural wrapping over hard character limits.
2. Keep list/table/code formatting clear and maintainable.
3. Do not reflow content solely to satisfy a fixed line-length target.

This overrides any local preference for 80-column Markdown wrap when the ParaDOCS plugin is active for Cursor guide and corpus authoring.
